2. **Transfer‑learning layer** – train a shallow multilayer perceptron (MLP) on the residuals (reference – physics‑predicted) from the collocated sites.  
3. **Domain adaptation** – apply unsupervised adversarial adaptation (e.g., DANN) to align the feature distributions of un‑calibrated nodes with those of the calibrated subset, allowing the MLP to be fine‑tuned on the broader network without additional ground truth.  
4. **Online update** – incorporate a recursive Kalman filter that adjusts the physics parameters in real time when short‑term reference data (e.g., mobile calibration campaigns) become available.  

