*Premise*: Urban air‑quality fields are governed by processes operating at distinct spatial and temporal scales—rapid micro‑scale emissions (traffic, point sources), mesoscale transport (wind corridors), and synoptic influences (regional aerosol loading). A graph‑based framework that respects these scales can fuse heterogeneous data streams (high‑frequency low‑cost sensors, medium‑resolution satellite AOD, sparse reference stations, traffic flow, meteorology) while providing calibrated uncertainty estimates.  

