| **1 – Pumpkin Patch Pop‑Up** | Mini‑pumpkin display from a nearby farm; free pumpkin‑shaped cookie for kids who bring a reusable bag. | Highlights local agriculture, eco‑friendly messaging. | Partner with **Farm Co‑Op**; set up a 4‑ft table outside. |
| **2 – Live Baking Demo** | Show how the Pumpkin‑Spice Croissant is made; attendees receive a 10 % off coupon for the sampler. | Gives a “behind‑the‑scenes” experience tourists love. | Schedule a 30‑min demo during the lunch rush; promote via Instagram Live. |
| **3 – Family Story Hour** | Local author reads a fall‑themed children’s book; families get a “Kids Eat Free” voucher (one pastry). | Draws parents with young children; creates repeat visits. | Coordinate with the **Downtown Library** for author outreach; set up a cozy corner with cushions. |
| **4 – Tourist Treasure Hunt** | Simple map linking nearby landmarks (historic clock tower, museum, boutique). Participants who visit all spots receive a stamped loyalty card redeemable for a free sampler. | Turns the bakery into a checkpoint on a downtown walking tour. | Print maps; collaborate with the **Tourist Information Center** for distribution. |

*Tip*: Rotate the events on the same weekday evenings (e.g., Thursday 5‑7 pm) to build a habit.

