### 1. Medical applications (disease treatment and prevention)

| Issue | Scientific background | Ethical implication |
|------|----------------------|---------------------|
| **Therapeutic potential** | Early‑phase trials (e.g., 2021 – 2022 studies on sickle‑cell disease, β‑thalassaemia, Leber congenital amaurosis) have shown >70 % of patients achieving clinically meaningful outcomes after a single in‑vivo CRISPR infusion. | *Beneficence*: the possibility of curing previously untreatable genetic disorders creates a strong moral imperative to pursue the technology. |
