*Premise*: The drift of electrochemical low‑cost sensors can be expressed as a combination of (i) a deterministic physics‑based response to temperature, relative humidity and sensor ageing, and (ii) a stochastic residual that varies with local pollutant mixtures. By training a compact neural‐network on a small set of co‑located reference‑grade stations and then applying domain‑adaptation techniques to the wider network, the model can inherit the physics‑based bias structure while learning site‑specific corrections.  

*Proposed method*:  
