| **Subscriber growth** | Monthly tally of paid passes | Indicates revenue trends. |
| **CO₂ reduction estimate** | Apply a standard factor (≈0.9 lb CO₂ saved per mile not driven) to total bike miles | Provides a simple environmental impact figure for reporting. |
| **User feedback** | Quarterly in‑app survey (rating of bike condition, safety, overall experience) | Guides service improvements. |

**Reporting:** Produce a short monthly dashboard (rides, revenue, CO₂ saved) for the city council and publish a quarterly summary on the program website for public transparency.

---

### Implementation Timeline (high‑level)

| Month | Milestone |
|-------|-----------|
| 1‑2 | Finalise site list, procure bikes and dock hardware, set up app backend. |
| 3‑4 | Install first wave of stations (transit hubs + campuses), train maintenance crew, launch marketing teaser. |
| 5   | Soft launch with free‑trial period; begin data collection. |
| 6   | Full launch of pricing tiers, corporate outreach, and safety‑education campaign. |
| 7‑12| Monitor usage, adjust station density where demand is high, release first impact report. |

---

**Bottom line:** By following this roadmap the city can roll out a functional bike‑share system that serves commuters, students, and local residents, while keeping costs manageable and providing enough data to expand or refine the service after the first year. --> Text length need to be between 0 and 5000 characters

