Consequently, negotiations would be marked by a mixture of *greater openness* (because the parties now see the mutual benefit of compromise) and *heightened emotional intensity* (because every clause is weighed against the specter of future bloodshed). This blend of strategic realism and moral pressure is precisely what would convert the historically punitive Versailles settlement into a more balanced, forward‑looking peace—while simultaneously immersing its architects in an unprecedented psychological burden. --> Text length need to be between 0 and 5000 characters

