- Integrate a micro‑fluidic nutrient‑sensor patch (ion‑selective and temperature) that monitors the immediate root microenvironment.  
- Deploy a lightweight edge‑AI that runs a rule‑based controller: when RH falls below 60 % or leaf‑temperature spikes > 2 °C above baseline, the controller sends a low‑frequency acoustic pulse (≈ 20 kHz) that has been shown to stimulate EPS production in *Pseudomonas*.  

